# Empty State & Startup Views

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

An empty state tells people a view has nothing in it yet, and what to do about it. A startup view tells them Home Assistant is still starting. Neither is an error, and neither should look like one.

This page covers:

- Empty State & Startup Views
  - `hui-empty-state-card`
  - `hui-starting-card`
  - Home Assistant Empty State Pattern

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

The Empty State card is centred in one card. From the top: an icon, a title, a sentence of content and a row of buttons. The content is at most 640 pixels wide and the buttons wrap on a narrow screen.

The starting view is a spinner above a single sentence: “Home Assistant is starting, please wait…”.

